     ```ts
     const EMAIL_PATTERN = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
     export function validateForm(form: BookingForm): BookingFormErrors {
       const errors: BookingFormErrors = {};
       if (form.firstName === '') errors.firstName = 'First name is required';
       else if (form.firstName.length < 2) errors.firstName = 'First name must be at least 2 characters';
       if (form.lastName === '') errors.lastName = 'Last name is required';
       else if (form.lastName.length < 2) errors.lastName = 'Last name must be at least 2 characters';
       if (form.email === '') errors.email = 'Email is required';
       else if (!EMAIL_PATTERN.test(form.email)) errors.email = 'Enter a valid email address';
       if (form.confirmEmail === '') errors.confirmEmail = 'Confirm email is required';
       else if (form.confirmEmail !== form.email) errors.confirmEmail = 'Email addresses do not match';
       if (form.phone !== '' && !/^\d{9}$/.test(form.phone)) errors.phone = 'Phone number must be exactly 9 digits';
       if (!form.terms) errors.terms = 'You must accept the terms and conditions';
       return errors;
     }
     ```

   - **apps/cinescope/src/pages/Checkout/FormTextField.tsx** (created) — reusable MUI `TextField` wrapper taking `label`/`labelTestId`/`inputTestId`/`errorTestId`/`value`/`error`/`showError`/`onChange`/`onBlur`; label rendered as `<span data-testid={labelTestId}>{label}</span>`; native input gets `slotProps={{ htmlInput: { 'data-testid': inputTestId } }}` (confirmed valid for MUI v9.4.0 via `TextField.d.ts` inspection); `helperText` only rendered (wrapped in a `data-testid={errorTestId}` span) when `showError && error` so the `-error` element only exists while the message is shown, per spec section 9.7.

   - **apps/cinescope/src/pages/Checkout/Checkout.tsx** (created) — uses `useTicketScreen()`; local `touched` state (all fields false initially, not persisted, per spec 7.1); `setField()` writes into `booking.form` via `updateBooking`; `markTouched()`; `handlePay()`: if `validateForm` finds any errors, sets all fields touched + shows toast `'The form contains errors'` and returns (no request sent); else sets `submitting=true`, calls `createReservation({screeningId, seats: items.flatMap(i=>i.seatIds), customer:{firstName,lastName,email,phone}, totalPrice: total})`; on success marks booking paid (`updateBooking(current => ({...current, paid:true, email: current.form.email}))`) and navigates to `/confirmation`; on failure resets `submitting=false` and shows toast `'Payment failed. Please try again.'`. Renders `checkout-title` (`"Your details"`), five `FormTextField`s (first/last name, email, confirm email, phone — required labels end in `' *'`, phone label does not), an MUI `Checkbox`+`FormControlLabel` for terms (`slotProps={{ input: { 'data-testid': 'terms-checkbox' } as never }}`, label `<span data-testid="terms-label">I accept the terms and conditions *</span>`, error line `terms-error` shown conditionally), `checkout-back-button` (→ summary route), and `pay-button` reading `` `Pay ${formatPrice(total)}` `` normally or `'Processing…'` while `submitting` (disabled while submitting).

   - **apps/cinescope/src/pages/Checkout/checkout.scss** (created).

   - **apps/cinescope/src/pages/Confirmation/Confirmation.tsx** (created) — on mount, loads booking; if missing or not `paid`, navigates to `/` (replace); else renders `confirmation-heading` (`"Payment successful"`), `confirmation-message` (`` `Your tickets will be sent shortly to ${booking.email}` ``), and `confirmation-continue-button` that clears the booking and navigates to `/`.

   - **apps/cinescope/src/pages/Confirmation/confirmation.scss** (created).

   - Pre-existing files read but **not modified**: `apps/cinescope/src/main.tsx` (ThemeProvider/CssBaseline/LocalizationProvider/BrowserRouter wrapping — left as-is), `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.spec.tsx` (default Nx-generated test, left as-is), `apps/cinescope/project.json`, `apps/cinescope/tsconfig.app.json`, `apps/cinescope/vite.config.mts`, `apps/cinescope/eslint.config.mjs`, `apps/cinescope/src/styles.scss`, root `package.json`, `tsconfig.base.json`, `nx.json`, `db.json` (viewed only — never edited, per explicit spec instruction "Do not edit db.json by hand").

   - **/tmp/cdp-drive.mjs** (created and iterated, outside the project — a disposable manual-testing script, not part of the app or its dependencies) — final working version launches headless Chromium, connects via raw CDP WebSocket, navigates directly to `http://localhost:4200/screenings/1/seats` (bypassing the date-gated movie list since the sandbox clock's "today" has no matching `db.json` screenings), selects 2 available seats + 1 available couch, continues to summary, confirms to checkout, fills the form via native-setter+dispatch-event `fillInput()`, checks the terms checkbox, clicks pay, and verifies arrival at the confirmation screen — capturing screenshots `/tmp/01-movie-list.png` through `/tmp/07-confirmation.png` and collecting any console errors/exceptions.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **ESLint non-null-assertion warnings (4 total, 0 errors)** in `ticketItems.ts` (×2), `MovieList.tsx`, `Summary.tsx`. Fixed by replacing `map.get(key)!` patterns with `(map.get(key) ?? [])` fallbacks, and in `Summary.tsx` by removing the unnecessary `!` since TS narrowing from the earlier `if (!booking) return null;` guard already proved `booking` non-null in the closure. Re-ran `pnpm nx lint cinescope` afterward — clean, 0 warnings/errors.
   - **`pnpm nx build cinescope` failure**: `[ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY] Aborted removal of modules directory due to no TTY`. Root cause: pnpm's automatic dependency-status check wanted to reinstall/purge `node_modules` but couldn't prompt for confirmation in a non-interactive shell. A plain `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` succeeded silently but didn't resolve the subsequent `nx build` invocation's own internal check. Fixed by running `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope`, which let pnpm auto-confirm the reinstall (recreated `node_modules`, reinstalled ~898 packages in 4.4s) and then proceeded to a successful Vite build ("✓ built in 264ms", "Successfully ran target build for project cinescope"). Subsequent plain `pnpm nx build cinescope` (without `CI=true`) then also succeeded without the error, suggesting the one-time reinstall resolved the underlying state mismatch.
   - **`curl: command not found`**: the sandbox has no `curl` binary. Switched to Node `fetch()`/`http.get()` for connectivity checks.
   - **Node `fetch()`/`http.get()` to `localhost:3000`/`127.0.0.1:3000` returning `ECONNREFUSED` / generic "fetch failed"**, despite the backend actually running: Diagnosed via an `EADDRINUSE` error (when attempting to start a second `json-server` instance) that revealed the existing instance was bound to `::1:3000` (IPv6) only. Confirmed working connectivity by explicitly forcing IPv6 in a Node `http.get({host:'::1', family:6, ...})` call, which successfully returned the `/movies` JSON payload. Concluded this was an artifact of my simplistic single-address test scripts lacking Happy-Eyeballs-style dual-stack retry, not a real application or server defect — real browsers (and the later CDP-driven headless Chromium) connect to `localhost:4200`/`localhost:3000` without issue.
   - **Background task tracking confusion**: initial `(nohup pnpm api > /tmp/api.log 2>&1 &)` / `(nohup pnpm nx serve cinescope > /tmp/serve.log 2>&1 &)` commands succeeded in starting the servers but weren't tracked as harness background tasks (no task ID), making it harder to introspect their state via the Bash tool's structured output. Subsequently also started proper `run_in_background: true` Bash invocations of `pnpm api` (task `bug2oazy3`) and `pnpm nx serve cinescope` (task `b6qe1z96u`) for better tracking; `bug2oazy3` failed immediately with `EADDRINUSE` (expected, since the nohup'd instance already owned port 3000) and `b6qe1z96u` printed `"Waiting for cinescope:serve in another nx process"` (also expected/benign, confirming the nohup'd dev server was already live on port 4200). No functional problem, just duplicate/overlapping server-start attempts; the original nohup'd instances remained the ones actually serving traffic throughout testing.
   - **No `chromium-cli` / Playwright npm package available** for the `run` skill's recommended "Browser-driven web app" testing pattern, and adding Playwright as a new dependency would conflict with the spec's "Do not add dependencies" rule for the app (and felt inappropriate even as a devDependency given that instruction's spirit). Resolved by hand-rolling a minimal CDP (Chrome DevTools Protocol) driver in a standalone `/tmp/cdp-drive.mjs` script using only Node builtins (`child_process`, `node:timers/promises`, `node:fs`, global `WebSocket`, global `fetch`) against the pre-installed Chromium binary at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome` — this lives entirely outside the project and adds no dependency to `package.json`.
   - **Sandbox "today" date (2026-10-16) outside db.json's screening date range (2026-09-15 to 2026-09-21)**: First smoke-test run against `http://localhost:4200/` showed 0 movie cards and no screening buttons — initially looked like a possible bug, but matched the spec's explicit callout exactly (section 2.2: "on other dates the movie list may show 'No screenings on this day' for every day it offers — that is expected. Do not change db.json, and do not change the date logic to see screenings."). Confirmed via screenshot `/tmp/01-movie-list.png` that the day-picker (Today/Saturday/Sunday/Monday/Tuesday + datepicker) and the "No screenings on this day" empty state both rendered correctly. A follow-up attempt to force a past date via `?date=2026-09-15` in the URL also correctly fell back to "today" per AC-55 ("a missing, invalid or past date selects today") — this is correct behavior, not a bug, since 2026-09-15 is before the sandbox's actual "today" of 2026-10-16. Resolved by pivoting the CDP driver to navigate directly to `/screenings/1/seats` (a route that loads a specific screening by id regardless of "today") to continue testing the deeper booking flow, since that route and its spec guards do not depend on the movie list's date filtering.

5. Problem Solving:
   - Successfully resolved the pnpm/nx build pipeline issue (via `CI=true`) and achieved a clean, warning-free `pnpm nx lint cinescope` and successful `pnpm nx build cinescope`.
   - Successfully worked around the sandbox's lack of browser-automation tooling by writing a from-scratch CDP driver, and used it to execute and verify an end-to-end booking flow (seat selection → summary → checkout → payment → confirmation) against the live dev server and backend, with zero console errors/exceptions reported.
   - Verified numerically that the auditorium renders exactly 296 `seat` elements + 12 `couch` elements = 308 selectable elements (matching AC-15), that selecting 2 seats + 1 couch correctly reports "Selected seats: 4" (couch counted as 2, matching AC-20), that the summary total (139.00 PLN) correctly sums the individual prices, that the pay button label format (`"Pay 139.00 PLN"`) matches spec, and that the confirmation message correctly embeds the submitted email address.
   - Visually confirmed via `/tmp/02-seat-map.png` that: the title/subtitle/seat-limit-info/SCREEN bar render correctly with the exact expected show-date string `"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00"`; row 1 shows accessible seats (columns 10–15) in the correct blue `#1565C0`; occupied seats from `db.json`'s `occupiedSeats` for screening 1 (`R3C7,R3C8,R3C9` and `R6C12,R6C13`) render in the correct red `#C62828`; all other visible seats render in the correct green `#2E7D32`; the entrance gap in rows 1–10 correctly shows no seats/numbers on the left side; row labels appear on both left and right edges.
   - Remaining/ongoing: full visual review of the rest of the captured screenshots (`03`–`07`) to confirm the legend, selected-seats panel formatting, summary item layout/fields, checkout form field labels/asterisks/layout, and the confirmation screen's final appearance, plus targeted functional checks not yet exercised by the smoke test (10-seat cap toast, invalid-form toast and touched-state marking, payment-failure toast/retry, Back/Cancel navigation preserving or clearing state as specified, booking persistence across reload, "remove last summary item redirects to seat map" behavior, and the route guards correctly redirecting to `/` when entering summary/checkout/confirmation without a valid matching booking).

6. All user messages:
   - The single, complete initial user instruction (verbatim): "Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the React application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds."
   - No further user messages were sent during this session; all subsequent conversation turns were my own tool invocations and system-generated tool results/notifications (e.g., background task completion notices), not user input. (Note: the task's own meta-instructions explicitly warn that such system notifications must never be mistaken for user acknowledgement or approval.)

7. Pending Tasks:
   - Complete visual/functional verification of the remaining flow screenshots (`/tmp/03-seats-selected.png`, `/tmp/04-summary.png`, `/tmp/05-checkout-empty.png`, `/tmp/06-checkout-filled.png`, `/tmp/07-confirmation.png`) and spot-check additional edge-case behaviors not yet exercised (10-seat max toast, invalid checkout form submission toast + touched marking, payment failure path, Back/Cancel navigation, reload persistence, route guard redirects, removing the last summary item).
